    {
      "at": "2026-11-20T18:00:37Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R1-F1",
      "reason": "Right: a title or excerpt may hold the text backslash-u, which JSON writes with a doubled backslash, so a rule for the whole reply cannot hold. The guarantee now covers the locators only, where text is copied into a command, and the plan also checks that a locator holds no newline or tab."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-11-20T18:02:36Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R2-F1",
      "reason": "Partly right. I read both specs: neither says anything about escaping apostrophes, so nothing in them contradicts the plan. But they also say nothing about the form of a locator, which will be true once this is built. I added one spec sentence to the scope and a step in the last increment."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-11-20T18:03:28Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R3-F1",
      "reason": "Right: the plan encoded the locators before hiding paths, so a known path with an apostrophe or a percent sign would no longer match the redaction and could leak. The order is now: hide paths in the raw text first, then encode. A criterion and a test cover a path inside a locator."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-11-20T18:03:28Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R3-F2",
      "reason": "Right: a heading that holds the text percent-27 must come back as exactly that after decoding, so the criterion now says the locator the engine gets equals the one it gave, with no claim that it has no codes."
    }
  ],
